---
description: Copy the Netlify deploy preview URL from the pull request and keep its double hyphen
alwaysApply: true
---

When a person needs a link to test this app, copy the deploy preview URL from the current pull request. Do not build the hostname yourself.

1. Read the pull request. Use the Deploy Preview link in the Netlify comment, or the `target_url` on the `netlify/.../deploy-preview` commit status.
2. Before sending it, check the hostname character by character. The preview name and the site name are separated by two hyphens: `deploy-preview-3--bubblewrapsheet.netlify.app`. One hyphen is a different hostname and Netlify reports it as site not found.
3. Paste the URL in inline code or a fenced block so Markdown cannot turn `--` into a dash.
4. `https://bubblewrapsheet.netlify.app/` is production. Do not send it as the preview.
